virglrenderer: ask for EXT_texture_shadow_lod only where it is needed

What: the extension was required whenever a shadow 2D array, cube or cube array
lookup had anything in its bias slot. That slot also holds the gradients of TXD,
the bias of TXB/TXB2 and the compare value of TEX2 and TG4. The extension is now
required only for what it adds: an explicit lod (TXL/TXL2) on these three
targets and a bias (TXB/TXB2) on 2D array and cube array shadow samplers.
texture(samplerCubeShadow, P, bias), textureGrad() and textureGather() with a
compare value are core GLSL (1.30/4.00) and ESSL 3.00/3.10.
Why: the Mac has no EXT_texture_shadow_lod and refused these shaders, which
stopped the guest's whole context (dEQP-GLES3 shaders.texture_functions:
texturegradoffset.*, texture.samplercubeshadow_bias_fragment; in one dEQP
process every later case failed).
Upstreamable; not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-core-glsl-shaders.c "textureGradOffset on a shadow array
sampler", "textureGrad on a shadow cube sampler", "texture() with a bias on a
shadow cube sampler", "textureGather on a shadow cube sampler" (fail without).
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_shader.c
@@ -3426,11 +3426,19 @@
 
    bool has_bias = strbuf_get_len (&bias_buf) != 0;
    bool has_offset = strbuf_get_len (&offset_buf) != 0;
-   // EXT_texture_shadow_lod defines a few more functions handling bias
+   // EXT_texture_shadow_lod adds an explicit lod for 2D array, cube and cube
+   // array shadow samplers, and a bias for 2D array and cube array ones. The
+   // other uses of bias_buf are core GLSL and ESSL 3.00: a bias on a cube
+   // shadow sampler, gradients (TXD), the compare value of TEX2 and TG4.
+   // Hosts without the extension (macOS) refuse a shader that asks for it.
+   bool is_lod = inst->Instruction.Opcode == TGSI_OPCODE_TXL ||
+                 inst->Instruction.Opcode == TGSI_OPCODE_TXL2;
+   bool is_bias = inst->Instruction.Opcode == TGSI_OPCODE_TXB ||
+                  inst->Instruction.Opcode == TGSI_OPCODE_TXB2;
    if (has_bias &&
-       (inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOW2D_ARRAY ||
-        inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE ||
-        inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE_ARRAY))
+       (((is_lod || is_bias) && (inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOW2D_ARRAY ||
+                                 inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE_ARRAY)) ||
+        (is_lod && inst->Texture.Texture == TGSI_TEXTURE_SHADOWCUBE)))
       ctx->shader_req_bits |= SHADER_REQ_TEXTURE_SHADOW_LOD;
 
    // EXT_texture_shadow_lod also adds the missing textureOffset for 2DArrayShadow in GLES
